 "notes": "Fig. 18 (left panel, 'Combined constraint' = constraint_combined_new.pdf in e-print, a raster image; extracted by color segmentation with axes calibrated on gridlines). Curve is the closed boundary of the pink shaded region: Scenario A (K_sigma=0, no modification to nuclear interactions), which the paper states is its conservative benchmark combined constraint from crust thermal relaxation, isolated NS cooling and pulsar glitches. Points traverse the polygon starting at the low-mass tip (~5e-10 eV), along the upper edge, across the plot's top boundary (region clipped at 1/f_a = 1e-9 GeV^-1), and back along the lower edge near the QCD line; mass is therefore not monotonic (2D excluded region). Cross-checks: lower edge corresponds to eps~0.17 and upper edge to eps~5.5e-7 for ma>1e-8 eV, matching Tables V and VII (eps = (ma*fa/5.7e6 eV*GeV)^2). No DM density assumption (astrophysical bound); paper quotes no statistical CL. Scenarios B/C (hatched) are stronger, non-benchmark variants and were not traced.",
